From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zetarancio <zetarancio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: rk817: clear SYS_CAN_SD to fix ~8 mA
 off-state drain

The RK817 PMIC's SYS_CAN_SD bit (bit 7 of CHRG_TERM, register 0xe6)
allows the charger block to autonomously cut the system power rail.
The BSP kernel unconditionally clears this bit during charger probe
(rk817_charge_sys_can_sd_disable), but the mainline driver never
touches it, leaving the hardware-default value (set) in place.

When SYS_CAN_SD is left set the charger monitoring circuitry remains
active after system-off, drawing ~8 mA from the battery.  Clearing the
single bit drops off-state drain to ~0.05 mA, matching stock firmware.

Signed-off-by: Zetarancio <zetarancio@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c | 10 ++++++++++
 include/linux/mfd/rk808.h            |  1 +
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/mfd/rk808.h b/include/linux/mfd/rk808.h
--- a/include/linux/mfd/rk808.h
+++ b/include/linux/mfd/rk808.h
@@ -1180,6 +1180,7 @@
 #define RK817_PMIC_CHRG_TERM		0xe6
 #define RK817_CHRG_TERM_ANA_DIG		(0x01 << 2)
 #define RK817_CHRG_TERM_ANA_SEL		(0x03 << 0)
+#define RK817_SYS_CAN_SD		(0x01 << 7)
 #define RK817_CHRG_EN			(0x01 << 6)
 
 #define RK817_PMIC_CHRG_STS		0xeb
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
@@ -1011,6 +1011,16 @@ static int rk817_battery_init(struct rk817_charger *charger,
 	chg_term_i_reg = (chg_term_ma - 100) / 100;
 	regmap_write_bits(rk808->regmap, RK817_PMIC_CHRG_TERM,
 			  RK817_CHRG_TERM_ANA_SEL, chg_term_i_reg);
 
+	/*
+	 * Clear SYS_CAN_SD to prevent the PMIC from autonomously cutting
+	 * the system power rail.  The BSP kernel always clears this bit
+	 * (rk817_charge_sys_can_sd_disable); mainline never touched it,
+	 * leaving the hardware default (set) in place.  When set, the
+	 * charger block stays active after system-off, causing ~8 mA drain.
+	 */
+	regmap_write_bits(rk808->regmap, RK817_PMIC_CHRG_TERM,
+			  RK817_SYS_CAN_SD, 0);
+
 	ret = rk817_read_or_set_full_charge_on_boot(charger, bat_info);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
-- 
